{#- ================== US BOTTOMING-WATCH LANE (W-A, restored) ==================
   The sixth strip of the US act board, sitting UNDER the five action lanes on the
   Sector Intelligence Overview (sector_central.html).

   WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. #4599 shipped this lane on sector_central because the
   cycle organ had written `b-gold_miners: phase=Trough, osc_slope=+1.3` while the
   board showed gold_miners on reduce/avoid — "the engine saw it; nothing the
   operator looks at said so". #4642 then transplanted the us_stocks five-lane
   board over sector_central's own five lanes; its summary called the board it
   replaced "the client-rendered 4-lane themes-only board", but the deleted code
   ran FIVE actLane() calls — buy, wait, trim, avoid, AND bottom. Both boards had
   five lanes, so the swap read as like-for-like and the bottoming lane went dark
   while engine/us_act_now.py and scripts/build_baskets.py kept computing and
   shipping its payload. This restores the display half. The engine, the builder,
   and the payload are untouched.

   LANE, NOT COLUMN. #4599's design note is "fifth lane under the existing four
   (they keep their 4-col geometry at every breakpoint)" — the bottoming lane has
   never been an action column. It is a WATCH surface: the five lanes above answer
   "what do I do", this one answers "what is forming". It spans the full grid width
   (grid-column: 1/-1) rather than squeezing the action lanes into a sixth column.

   COPY LAW (F1/W8-R3, doctrine Law 1-2). Watch vocabulary only, never a buy verb.
   Two payload fields are deliberately NEVER rendered here — `signal` ("BUY") and
   `timing_state` (whose real vocabulary includes the literal "FRESH BUY").
   The cycle organ's registered output is instead quoted as the fixed phrase
   "cycle turn signal — watch only", with its trend-gate conflict printed beside
   it. tests/test_us_act_now.py pins that fence against this file.

   The lane's fixed wording is authored HERE; its disclosures ship from the engine
   (`bottoming_authority`) so the page cannot drift from the measured basis. An
   older artifact without the authority block renders no disclosure rather than a
   blank one. Hover copy rides data-tip-en/data-tip-zh — never a translated HTML
   title attribute, which the language switch cannot reach (house law, CI-guarded).
   That fence greps this file for the literal attribute spelling, so do not write it
   out even inside a comment: the guard cannot tell prose from markup.

   Host contract: sector_central passes `bottoming` = theme_intel.act_now sliced to
   {bottoming_watch, dual_read_ids, recovering_ids, bottoming_authority}. Absent or
   empty → the strip self-hides. t()/tr() come from the host Jinja env. -#}
{#- Marks are monoline icons, never emoji (doctrine §5.8). The strip borrows the
    board's .acth-icon / .ai-bdg wrappers, so the sizing + stroke rules already
    shipped by _us_act_now_board.html.j2 (its host) cover these two marks — no
    icon CSS is added here. -#}
{% from "_icons.html.j2" import icon %}
{#- `is defined` is load-bearing: the same board include renders on us_stocks.html
    via dashboard.html.j2, where no bottoming payload is passed. Default Undefined is
    falsy so `bottoming and ...` already short-circuits, but the explicit guard keeps
    the strip self-hiding if a host ever switches to StrictUndefined. -#}
{%- if bottoming is defined and bottoming and bottoming.get('bottoming_watch') is not none -%}
{%- set _bw_rows = bottoming.get('bottoming_watch') or [] -%}
{%- set _bw_auth = bottoming.get('bottoming_authority') or {} -%}
{#- Both id spellings ride the set ('b-uranium_miners' and 'uranium_miners'), so a
    row matches whichever namespace produced it. -#}
{%- set _bw_dual = bottoming.get('dual_read_ids') or [] -%}
  <style>
  /* Bottoming watch — the act board's watch strip. Reuses the V2 lane chrome
     (.actcol/.acth/.actitem/.ab-chip) verbatim; the only additions are the
     full-width span and the internal row grid, because this strip is as wide as
     the whole board rather than one column. Rides with the include for the same
     reason the board CSS does: editing theme.css rehashes it and stales the ?v=
     stamp on ~176 committed pages. */
  .actcol.act-bottom { grid-column: 1 / -1; --act-accent: var(--info); --act-accent-ink: var(--ink-info, var(--info)); }
  .abw-rows { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 0 12px; padding: 6px 0; }
  @media (max-width: 900px) { .abw-rows { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); } }
  /* The turn reading sits right of the name, like .act-row-score on a theme row.
     Info-toned, NOT green: a rising oscillator on a watch lane is a state, not an
     endorsement, and green here would read as the buy verb this lane must not carry. */
  .abw-turn { flex: none; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
              white-space: nowrap; color: var(--ink-info, var(--info)); cursor: help; }
  .abw-foot { padding: 8px 13px 10px; border-top: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--line) 55%, transparent);
              font-size: 10.5px; line-height: 1.5; color: var(--muted); }
  .abw-foot p { margin: 0 0 4px; }
  .abw-foot p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  </style>
  <div class="actcol act-bottom" id="ab-bottom">
    <div class="acth">
      <div class="acth-title-row">
        {#- `coil` — converging lines then a turn up: compression resolving, which is
            exactly what this strip watches. The five action lanes above already take
            target / clock / accel / profits / hold. -#}
        <span class="acth-icon">{{ icon('coil') }}</span>
        <span class="acth-name"><span class="l-en">Bottoming watch</span><span class="l-zh">筑底观察</span></span>
        <span class="acth-count">{{ _bw_rows | length }}</span>
      </div>
      <div class="acth-sub"><span class="l-en">cycle lows forming — watch, don't chase</span><span class="l-zh">周期底部形成中——观察，勿追</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="actbody">
      {%- if _bw_rows %}
      <div class="abw-rows">
        {%- for x in _bw_rows %}
        {#- Dual read (FT-R1): this row also sits on reduce/avoid. Both reads are
            shown rather than picking one — the chip names the disagreement. -#}
        {%- set _dual = (x.id in _bw_dual) or (x.cid in _bw_dual) -%}
        <a class="actitem" data-rpop href="{{ x.href }}">
          <span class="act-row-top">
            <span class="ai-bdg">{{ icon('diamond') if x.kind == 'BASKET' else icon('sector') }}</span>
            <span class="act-row-name"><span class="l-en">{{ x.name | e }}</span><span class="l-zh">{{ (x.name_zh or x.name) | e }}</span></span>
            {%- if x.osc_slope is not none %}
            <span class="abw-turn" data-tip-en="Momentum is turning up from the low — a bigger number is a sharper turn. A first hint, not a buy signal." data-tip-zh="动能正从低位回升——数字越大转向越明显。仅是初步迹象，非买入信号。">&#8599; {{ '%.1f'|format(x.osc_slope) }}</span>
            {%- endif %}
          </span>
          {%- if x.cycle_signal or x.gate_conflict or _dual %}
          <span class="act-row-chips">
            {#- The cycle organ's own registered output, quoted as such. The raw
                field is never printed: its vocabulary is a buy verb. -#}
            {%- if x.cycle_signal %}<span class="ab-chip ab-chip--info" data-tip-en="The cycle model registered a turn on this name. It is shown as the model's own output, quoted — this lane is watch-only and never a buy signal." data-tip-zh="周期模型对该名称登记了一次转折。此处按模型自身输出原样引用——本栏仅供观察，绝非买入信号。"><span class="l-en">cycle turn signal — watch only</span><span class="l-zh">周期转折信号——仅观察</span></span>{% endif -%}
            {%- if x.gate_conflict %}<span class="ab-chip ab-chip--warn" data-tip-en="The cycle read turned up, but price is still below its 200-day trend — the longer-term gate has not opened. The two disagree; both are shown." data-tip-zh="周期读数已转升，但价格仍低于200日趋势线——长期闸门尚未打开。两者判读不一致，并列显示。"><span class="l-en">below 200-day trend — gate shut</span><span class="l-zh">低于200日趋势——闸门关闭</span></span>{% endif -%}
            {%- if _dual %}<span class="ab-chip ab-chip--warn" data-tip-en="The longer trend still says reduce, but the cycle read shows a low forming. This name also appears on the Reduce / Stand aside lanes above — both reads are shown so you can see the disagreement." data-tip-zh="长期趋势仍建议减仓，但周期读数显示底部正在形成。该名称同时出现在上方的减仓／观望栏——两种判读并列显示，便于看清分歧。"><span class="l-en">may be bottoming</span><span class="l-zh">或正筑底</span></span>{% endif -%}
          </span>
          {%- endif %}
          {%- if x.pos is not none %}
          <span class="act-row-stat"><span class="l-en">position in cycle range</span><span class="l-zh">周期区间位置</span> <b>{{ '%.0f'|format(x.pos) }}</b>/100</span>
          {%- endif %}
        </a>
        {%- endfor %}
      </div>
      {%- else %}
      <p class="muted sm" style="padding:10px 13px"><span class="l-en">no basing candidates tonight</span><span class="l-zh">今晚无筑底候选</span></p>
      {%- endif %}
    </div>
    {#- Disclosures ship from the engine, printed only when they describe something
        actually on the page: the honest null when the lane has rows, the graduation
        note only when a recovering chip was rendered on the board above. -#}
    {%- if (_bw_rows and _bw_auth.get('null_disclosure_en')) or (bottoming.get('recovering_rendered') and _bw_auth.get('recovering_disclosure_en')) %}
    <div class="abw-foot">
      {%- if _bw_rows and _bw_auth.get('null_disclosure_en') %}
      <p><span class="l-en">{{ _bw_auth.get('null_disclosure_en') }}</span><span class="l-zh">{{ _bw_auth.get('null_disclosure_zh') or _bw_auth.get('null_disclosure_en') }}</span></p>
      {%- endif %}
      {%- if bottoming.get('recovering_rendered') and _bw_auth.get('recovering_disclosure_en') %}
      <p><span class="l-en">{{ _bw_auth.get('recovering_disclosure_en') }}</span><span class="l-zh">{{ _bw_auth.get('recovering_disclosure_zh') or _bw_auth.get('recovering_disclosure_en') }}</span></p>
      {%- endif %}
    </div>
    {%- endif %}
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
